{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '3\\\\.2|3\\\\.5|AX143|\\\\bL1\\\\b|[Ll]abel fitting|labels hidden' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md && rg --files reviews/2026-11-18/impl | rg 'layout|design-pass-1|docs\\\\.report' \"","aggregated_output":"docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:5:This plan builds the product defined in [02-product-spec.md](02-product-spec.md). Criterion IDs (F1, L1, A2, DX4, P1 …) refer to that spec; finding IDs (R5, D2 …) refer to [01-landscape.md](01-landscape.md).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:103:| `strict`, `onDiagnostic` | Diagnostics delivery (section 3.5 of the spec). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:132:The registry, with each code's level and outcome, is in the spec (section 3.5). Example for the Phase 1 combined dirty fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`):\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:186:| layout | Plot rectangle, tick sets, label boxes, legend and control placement | Implements L1, L3, L8. Takes a text-measurement interface as input. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:298:- Title, `labelledBy`, subtitle, axis titles; toolbar with legend toggles; full tooltip and fixed readout (I1); label fitting (L1) and the too-small fallback (L8); states (L7); reference lines and bands.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:302:- L1's property test in three engines, including text-spacing overrides and a late-loading font, on a category-axis line chart with long labels.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:327:- `bars` fixture: starts at zero, long label handled by L1's remedies, missing bar distinct from zero.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:375:| Property | fast-check | Invariants that must hold for any data: F1, F2, F5, F7, F11, L1. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:391:| DOM text costs too much with many charts on a page. | P5 is measured in M1. A fallback to canvas-drawn tick labels would give up user text spacing and forced-colors adaptation for those labels, so it must pass the same L1 and A6 tests before it is allowed. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:405:| Annotations beyond reference lines and bands | Text placement interacts with L1. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:96:| F3 | Input that cannot be plotted as given is reported, never guessed. The diagnostic registry (section 3.5) fixes each case's level, what is drawn and what the reader sees. | One test per code; the combined `dirty` fixture and the four one-bad-value fixtures yield exactly the codes listed in section 3.5 | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:107:### 3.2 Legibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:173:| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:225:| DX4 | Diagnostics follow the registry in section 3.5: stable code, chart name, field and rows where they apply, the fix, and a documentation page per code. | Message snapshots; link checker | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:262:| Diagnostics are a first-class feature with codes | R5: none of the ten named the field, the row or the problem. | Kept. Severity and delivery rewritten (3.5): readers are told too, and production builds are not silent. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:267:| Label fitting is a tested invariant with a visible fallback | R2. | Changed. The absolute \"everything always fits\" was infeasible in a 240 px tile; it is now \"nothing overlaps, and nothing disappears without the reader being told\". Rotation comes before truncation. |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/design-pass-1.events.jsonl\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.report.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.prompt.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/design-pass-1.report.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.fix.prompt.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout-fix-2.report.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/design-pass-1.prompt.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.report.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout-fix-2.prompt.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.events.jsonl\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.fix.report.md\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.fix.events.jsonl\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout-fix-2.events.jsonl\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.report.md reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/design-pass-1.report.md && rg -n -A 16 -B 3 'Where the library, spec and plan disagree' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.report.md && cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout-fix-2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.report.md reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/design-pass-1.report.md && rg -n -A 16 -B 3 'Where the library, spec and plan disagree' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.report.md && cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout-fix-2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"Implemented both modules in the owned directories.\n\n- [Simplified drawing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/simplify/index.ts) preserves run breaks, isolated points, and per-column extrema. It packs line, point, and area geometry and lets adjacent bands share a packed boundary when their projections and slot states match.\n- [Plot layout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts) computes projections, fits tick labels and titles, and reports `AX142` for small plots and `AX143` for hidden labels. It also handles compact, ring, message, and unmeasured layouts.\n- Added [simplification tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/simplify/simplify.test.ts) and [layout tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts) with fixed fixtures and fast-check properties.\n\n`npm run typecheck` passed. The million-slot cases took **20.0–25.2 ms** across three widths at DPR 1 and 2. The full `npm test` run ended with:\n\n```text\n Test Files  12 passed (12)\n      Tests  135 passed (135)\n   Start at  02:11:01\n   Duration  1.76s (tests 79%, transform 12%, import 7%, worker 1%)\n```\n\nThe density calculation counts partially covered device columns. The four-sample cap applies once simplification starts, as sparse series keep every value. The fixed slot join rule governs gaps even across empty columns. `fit.hidden` counts labels omitted after candidate thinning.\n\nNo contract changes are needed. Browser rendering, resize behavior, and accessibility were outside the Node verification.Updated `layout`, `view`, and `scene` and added regression tests before the fixes. All 111 tests in those modules passed.\n\n| # | Done | Regression coverage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Wrap before rotating | Yes | The seven-bar chart wraps only the long category to three lines. The existing two-line case still passes. [Layout tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts:223) |\n| 2. Use up to 40% for rotated labels | Yes | The same rotated label stays whole in a tall container and truncates in a shorter one. [Layout test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts:251) |\n| 3. Keep tick labels 6 px from axes | Yes | Checks both axes in both bar orientations. [Layout test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts:269) |\n| 4. Place reference labels | Yes in layout | Tests cover line and band placement, overlap, clipping, and middle truncation. Core still needs to pass `view.references` and `view.xDomain` into layout and include references in the layout cache key. This needs no shared contract change. [Layout tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts:280) |\n| 5. Order horizontal bars top to bottom | Yes | Checks that the first, middle, and last bars align with their category labels. [Scene test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts:161) |\n| 6. Round numeric scatter x outward | Yes | Checks `[10, 998]` becomes `[0, 1000]` and covers positive-only data, author bounds, zoom, and dates. [View test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/view/view.test.ts:137) |\n| 7. Style reference rules above marks | No, partially done | Tests confirm that rules draw over bars and areas with a 1.5 px stroke and `[4, 3]` dashes. The `[6, 3]` contrast pattern needs `RuleMark.dash` widened to accept `DashStyle` and both renderers updated to select the active pattern. [Scene tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts:250) |\n\nCategory wrapping uses word boundaries. A band spanning the plot gets a label just inside its edge when both outside positions are clipped.\n\n`npm run typecheck` passed. The first full test run failed on an out-of-scope linear-scale property test with seed `243009428`. The rerun passed. Browser and gallery output remain unverified. [Scale test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/scale/linear.test.ts:130)\n\n```text\n Test Files  33 passed (33)\n      Tests  495 passed (495)\n   Start at  03:20:34\n   Duration  2.25s (tests 81%, transform 9%, import 9%, worker 1%)\n```34-\n35-The DX10 test uses the built `packages/*/dist` files, not a packed tarball as spec DX10 says. Scripts in the `.html` examples are checked with `checkJs` and `strictNullChecks: false`, so `querySelector` needs no guards; `.ts` and `.tsx` examples are fully strict.\n36-\n37:### Where the library, spec and plan disagree\n38-1. **Spurious AX143 and \"Some labels hidden\" note on time and date axes.** `layout/labels.ts:142` counts repeated tick text from denser candidate tick sets as hidden labels (inferred from the code, not traced). Observed:\n39-   - the `dates.ts` instants chart at 752 px in America/Los_Angeles;\n40-   - the AX111 minimal input in UTC;\n41-   - `line-time.ts` at phone width;\n42-   - `units.ts` at 364 px, where all four month labels are visible.\n43-\n44-   This contradicts spec L1, where thinning is the remedy for these axes.\n45-2. **AX108 on the only series** shows the empty state \"No data to show.\" instead of an error state or a visible \"could not be drawn\". Only the summary says it. Spec 3.5, line 150.\n46-3. **Event values on a date axis.** The `zoom` event and `Point.x` give epoch milliseconds, while `controller.ts:751` says the window is given \"as the author would write it\". I documented what I observed and made the examples read both forms.\n47-4. **Script-tag file names.** Plan line 147 says `axylo.js` and `axylo.min.js`; the build makes `axylo.iife.js` and `axylo.iife.min.js` (`scripts/build.mjs:11-12`).\n48-5. **AX199 wording.** The message says it is \"a defect in Axylo, not in your data\" (`registry.ts:147`), but `validate()` also raises it when reading a row throws (`core/stages.ts:171-172`).\n49-6. **Title element.** Plan line 221 shows an `<h3>`; the built chart uses `div role=\"heading\"`.\n50-7. **Plan 1.6 message examples** differ from the registry wording. The registry is what the docs follow.\n51-8. **Zoom on category axes.** The type matrix says zoom \"Yes\" for line and area; I3 limits zoom to time, date and number x. I documented I3, which matches the built behaviour.\n52-9. **Typing with `strictNullChecks: false`.** Wide `y: [{ field, label }]` fails to type-check (TypeScript 7.0.2, seen in a probe). Spec 2.3 promises TypeScript 5.4+ with no strictness condition.\n53-10. **Smaller observations:**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
