le: { chart: 'Sessions' },\n    input: `target.style.width = '110px';\napps/docs/data/diagnostics.mjs:352:    code: 'AX143', level: 'hint', title: 'Labels hidden after every remedy',\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts:217:diagnostic('bar', { code: 'AX143', level: 'hint', effect: 'none', name: 'discloses hidden labels after fitting unordered categories', fix: /horizontal bars/i },\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts:67:        expect(codes(r).filter(code => code !== 'AX143')).toEqual(['AX111']);\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md:116:### F3 AX143 guidance\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md:118:> If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars.\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md:120:- **F3 bar: AX143 discloses hidden labels after fitting unordered categories**  \npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md:121:  The 90 bars and the note were present. The diagnostic said “Give the plot more room or shorten the labels.” Expected the horizontal-bar remedy. The [AX143 registry message](../../src/diagnostics/registry.ts#L130) omits it.\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md:194:- Month and year dates keep their input granularity. An IANA alias returned by the platform names the same zone. An unambiguous majority temporal kind sets the axis, and incompatible rows are diagnosed. In the zoned bar fixture, AX143 is a separate label-fitting warning. The temporal checks still require AX111 and exact local date/time readouts.\npackages/axylo/test/acceptance/EVIDENCE.json:115:  {\"criterion\":\"F3\",\"type\":\"bar\",\"file\":\"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts\",\"title\":\"F3 bar: AX143 discloses hidden labels after fitting unordered categories\"},\npackages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:217:  'viewAsTable', 'hideTable', 'noData', 'noObservation', 'incompleteStack', 'moreRows', 'otherSlices', 'valuesNotShown', 'valuesChanged', 'labelsHidden',\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
