zone }).format(value) });\n  });\n  for (const extra of disambiguators(zone)) {\n    const repeated = repeatedBuiltIn(ticks, builtIn, keys);\n    if (repeated.length === 0) break;\n    for (const j of repeated) {\n      fields[j] = { ...fields[j], ...extra };\n      ticks[j] = { value: ticks[j]!.value, label: dateTimeFormat(options.locale, { ...fields[j], timeZone: zone }).format(ticks[j]!.value) };\n    }\n  }\n  return ticks;\n}\n\n/**\n * Indexes of built-in labels that equal another label read in the same context. \"3:00 AM\" on two different\n * days is not repeated (the date is written where the day changes); \"1:00 AM\" twice on one day (a fold) is.\n */\nfunction repeatedBuiltIn(ticks: readonly Tick[], builtIn: readonly boolean[], keys: readonly number[]): number[] {\n  const id = (i: number): string => `${keys[i]}\\u0000${ticks[i]!.label}`;\n  const count = new Map<string, number>();\n  ticks.forEach((_, i) => count.set(id(i), (count.get(id(i)) ?? 0) + 1));\n  const out: number[] = [];\n  ticks.forEach((_, i) => {\n    if (builtIn[i] && (count.get(id(i)) ?? 0) > 1) out.push(i);\n  });\n  return out;\n}\nimport type { BandScale, Tick, TickCandidates } from '../core/contracts';\n\n/**\n * Bands of equal width. `padding` is the fraction of a step left empty, the same between bands and at both\n * ends, so the outer gaps match the inner ones. The range may run backwards (a vertical category axis\n * drawn top to bottom from a bottom origin); `map` always returns the lower pixel edge of the band, so a\n * rectangle at map(i) with width `bandwidth` covers it either way.\n */\nexport function bandScale(count: number, range: readonly [number, number], padding: number): BandScale {\n  const n = Number.isFinite(count) ? Math.max(0, Math.floor(count)) : 0;\n  const p = Number.isFinite(padding) ? Math.min(Math.max(padding, 0), 0.95) : 0;\n  const r0 = range[0];\n  const r1 = range[1];\n  const extent = Math.abs(r1 - r0);\n  const forward = r1 >= r0;\n  const step = n =