{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'same|duplicate|first|repeated' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.{fix.report,review,report}.md && git status --short -- packages/axylo/src/layout packages/axylo/test/layout packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts\"","aggregated_output":"reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:1:Review of packages/axylo/src/simplify/**, src/layout/** and their tests, against reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.prompt.md. Reviewer: Claude (same provider as any Claude author, so this is not a cross-provider review).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:47:- Fix: accept a truncation only if no other label on the axis has the same prefix and suffix. Otherwise keep more of the label, and if it cannot fit, hide it and count it.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:52:- Observed (ran): `too-small`. The left margin is 4 + 4 + 96 + 20, which leaves a plot 112 px wide. Without the title, the same input gives a plot 137 px wide.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:62:  - The message and compact results show the same problem.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:81:- Observed (ran): `joinRuns([V,V,NULL,V,V], {start:1,end:5})` reports `isolated:[1]`, although slot 1 is joined to slot 0. In the same way, `[V,V,NULL,V,NO_ROW,V]` with `{0,4}` reports `isolated:[3]`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:87:- Observed (ran, warm): 20.7–22.7 ms per call in Node at widths 97, 320, 877 and 1920, and DPR 1, 2 and 3. Under vitest the printed times are 23–49 ms. A single fused loop with the same per-column rule runs in about 4.5 ms on this machine.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:88:- Cause: both scans call `mapX` and `Math.floor` for every value. The first scan always maps pixels, even when the result will not be dense.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:117:- Where: labels.ts:180-186 (duplicates count as conflicts at every stage) and `middleText`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:121:- This matters for time or number ticks whose formatter produces the same text twice.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:122:- Fix: hide later duplicates (counted in `hidden`) instead of changing their text, and do not let them force remedies on the other labels.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:132:- **Simplify fidelity (F5, F2):** no failures found. I checked per-column first/min/max/last with ties, extremes at run ends, several runs in one column, value/null alternating within a pixel, NO_ROW joined versus NULL/INVALID/GAP/ABSENT_FIELD breaking, ranges starting or ending mid-run, negative pixels, an offset plot edge, DPR 1/1.5/2/3, NaN `mapX`, Float32 y, and the density threshold at 8 versus 9 values over 2 columns. My oracle found 0 mismatches in 3,000 cases.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.review.md:135:- **Areas:** no failures found. Both boundaries start and end at the same x in every run, bands split exactly where the join rule forbids joining, and a shared edge is the identical array when the sources match. Crossing and zero-height bands cause no index errors.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.fix.report.md:19:| 13. Blank and duplicate labels | Yes | Yes | Blank labels and later duplicates count as hidden on both axes without triggering remedies |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/layout.fix.report.md:36:The scoped TypeScript check and API examples check passed. Root `npm run typecheck` reported one error in the [scatter lookup fixture](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:10), which omits the required `DatumRef.x` field. All five root test failures came from that same out-of-scope file. Browser tests were outside this run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
